{
  "_comment": "Hook entries for the Stop event and whether each runs `ironmem hook stop` on a non-plugin install. Read by doctor's unit tests (crates/ironmem/src/doctor/hooks.rs, via include_str!) and by scripts/test_install_ironmem.py, so doctor and the installer are pinned to the same answers; both also run every row with `stop` swapped for each of the four hook names. A row without `args` is shell form; a row with `args` (whatever its value) carries it into the entry as is. A run whose program or wrapper-script word uses ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT} is `wired: false`: Claude Code leaves that variable unset for a settings.json hook (measured on 2.1.329). The installer does not count it; doctor matches it but reads it as not starting, which is what its side of these rows checks. `env_rows` are settings.json `env` values (`env` absent: no env key) and whether the Stop hook the installer wires then mines: `unset` (no string IRONMEM_MCP_MODE, so the launch environment decides), `writes` (a mode that writes) or `does_not_write`.",
